  "rules": [
    "Model forecasts exhibit a persistent downward bias relative to true outcomes, consistently underestimating price levels by approximately 10-15 EUR over the 30-day horizon.",
    "Forecasts display significant mean reversion lag; when recent history shows a strong upward trend (e.g., Example 4 and 5), the model fails to capture the momentum and predicts a slow, flat recovery instead of an accelerated spike.",
    "Sentiment spikes (values > 0.4) in the immediate past are ignored by the model, resulting in forecasts that do not react to positive market sentiment even when price action supports higher levels.",
    "The model suffers from 'overshoot avoidance' during volatility events; it predicts a smooth, linear path through high-volatility periods where true outcomes show sharp peaks followed by corrections (e.g., Example 1 and 2).",
    "When the last 3 days of history are above 54 EUR, the model's forecast trajectory remains flat or slightly declining, failing to extrapolate the upward trend seen in the true outcome."
  ]
}
